# The run ledgers ARE the evidence. The benchmark page states that its report is a pure
# function of the committed ledger and the corpus: CI re-derives every rate from the ledger with
# the standard library on each push, and `report.py --check` is the full proof, run locally
# (ADR-0074 keeps pipeline scripts out of CI). Either way the ledger has to be in the repository
# for that claim to mean anything. They are 260 KB in total, including the two superseded runs
# that record what the instrument got wrong.
build/
tools/portability/node_modules/
tools/portability/site/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/public/data/
tools/visual-verify/node_modules/
tools/visual-verify/screenshots/
# `tsc -b` rewrites this on every build; tracking it dirtied the tree after each one.
